{
  "id": "COMPOUND:16211 - PROTEIN:2332",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Paeonilide may interact with the phosphatidylinositol transfer protein alpha isoform, through a series of target-mediated pathways. Paeonilide is implicated in targeting the T-cell surface glycoprotein CD3 zeta chain, which is a key component of the T-cell receptor complex. This target is also a known target of (+)-Parviflorol and Jasplakinolide Z1, both of which are known to inhibit phosphatidylinositol transfer protein alpha isoform activity. The presence of multiple pathways linking Paeonilide to the phosphatidylinositol transfer protein alpha isoform suggests a possible role in modulating cellular processes involving this protein, potentially through the inhibition of phosphatidylinositol transfer activity. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Paeonilide and the phosphatidylinositol transfer protein alpha isoform, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
